<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>2.9.4: Making Sense of Inequalities and Their Solutions</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m00524</md:content-id>
    <md:title>2.9.4: Making Sense of Inequalities and Their Solutions</md:title>
    <md:uuid>7660b5bf-aa7c-4ee3-9bac-50247616417b</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section>
      <para>Use this information to answer questions 1 - 2.</para>
      <para>
        <quote>To help pay for his tuition, a college student plans to work in the evenings and on weekends. He has been offered two part-time jobs: working in the guest-services department at a hotel and waiting tables at a popular restaurant.</quote>
        <quote>The equation \( 7.50h + \frac {50}{4}h = 18h + 33 \) represents a possible constraint about a situation for 1 month.</quote>
     </para>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q #1-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Solve the equation and check your solution.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer: \( h=16.5 \)</para>
          <para>\( 7.50h + \frac {50}{4}h = 18h + 33 \)</para>
          <para>\( 7.50(16.5) + \frac {50}{4}(16.5) = 18(16.5) + 33 \)</para>
          <para>\(123.75+206.25=297+33\)</para>
          <para>\(330=330 \checkmark\)</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!--Q#2-->
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Add a scale on the number line so that the point marked with a circle represents the solution to the equation you found in question 1.
        <figure><media alt="A blank number line is shown with an open circle on a point in the middle.&#10;        "><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_01.svg"/></media></figure></para>
            <para>When you have finished graphing, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
            <figure>
              <media alt=" A number line is shown from 14 to 19 with an &#10;open circle on 16.5.&#10;">
                <image mime-type="image/jpeg" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_02.jpg"/>
              </media>
            </figure>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </example>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!-- END CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <title>Activity</title>
        <exercise id="_29538925-54ad-4d51-8b1a-d3614dd56a74" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which job pays better if he works fewer hours than the solution you found in question 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Hotel Job.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is the hotel job.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q #4-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Explain how you know.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The hotel job pays better if he works fewer than 16.5 hours a month because I found the pay for both jobs using numbers that are less than 16.5 and found that pay at the hotel job is always higher.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!-- BEGIN ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <section class="check-understanding">
        <exercise id="_7105cfee-99ee-4db0-9d8f-4882349ffbd7" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem>
            <para>Which job pays better if he works more hours than the solution you found in question 1?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Correct! Restaurant Job.</para>
            <para>The correct answer is the restaurant job.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--END ACTIVITY DROP DOWN 1 TRY -->
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <!--Q #6-->
      <exercise>
        <problem>
          <para>Explain how you know.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution>
          <para>Compare your answer:</para>
          <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample. The restaurant job pays better if he works more than 16.5 hours a month because I found the pay for both jobs using numbers that are more than 16.5 and found that pay at the restaurant job is always higher.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <!-- BEGIN CLICK TO REVEAL NO TEXTBOX -->
      <!--Q#7-->
      <example>
        <exercise>
          <problem>
            <para>Draw a number line, including a scale, so that the point marked with a circle represents the solution to the inequality: \( 7.50h + \frac {50}{4}h &lt; 18h + 33 \).
        <figure><media alt="A blank number line is shown with an open circle on a point in the middle.&#10;        "><image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_02_11_09_03.svg"/></media></figure></para>
            <para>Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution>
            <para>Compare your answer:</para>
            <para>Your answer may vary, but here is a sample.</para>
